  "research": "Wide grip: hands ~0.62 m apart (about 1.5x shoulder width), palms up (axis [1,0,0], tilt 0 so the bar runs square through both fists; place_bars puts the bar through both fist centres). Upper arm elev 15 / plane 53: hand x = 0.22 + 0.6 sin15 cos53 = 0.31, y = 0.6 sin15 sin53 = 0.12 (bar in front of the thighs). Elbows stay at the sides; forearm folds forward and a little out (bend [0.15,1,0]) so the hands stay wide at the top. Fixed curl bar (1.1 m shaft, small plates) so the camera can frame the athlete."
